    introTranscript: "Most of the problems that reach a desk in this division are simple enough to fix once. A form is wrong, a link is broken, a deadline was miscalculated. The problems that stay are different. They come back after a reasonable fix, they look different depending on who describes them, and everyone involved is acting sensibly. This module is about that second kind. It gives you a way to write the issue as a question instead of as a verdict, four lines of inquiry to run across it, three kinds of evidence to weigh against each other, and an hour-long team case consultation that examines the work without putting any individual person in the record. It does not decide anything. It gets an issue into a shape the office that holds the decision can actually act on.",
